docs/adr/0015 §6: a gate that has never been seen failing is not a
gate. One test, one wrong assertion, no database/app/fixture touched,
so it fails cleanly and immediately — proof material for
gates/test.sh, not a real regression.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SyvjibsMaMMeqKhNxadYFz
---
 app/backend/tests/test_fixture_failing.py | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 app/backend/tests/test_fixture_failing.py

diff --git a/app/backend/tests/test_fixture_failing.py b/app/backend/tests/test_fixture_failing.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e8a2d0e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/backend/tests/test_fixture_failing.py
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# docs/adr/0015 §6 fixture ("failing-test"): a deliberately, minimally wrong
+# assertion, nothing else — no database, no app, no fixture argument — so it
+# fails cleanly and immediately, not flakily or by environment. It proves
+# gates/test.sh actually rejects a bad input; it is never meant to pass.
+def test_fixture_deliberately_fails() -> None:
+    assert 1 == 2
